1
00:00:09,455 --> 00:00:13,918
KOCHIKAME

2
00:00:14,127 --> 00:00:17,004
Ah, summer's here again

3
00:00:17,213 --> 00:00:19,924
It's come, it's arrived, it's here

4
00:00:20,133 --> 00:00:23,010
Ah, summer's here again

5
00:00:23,219 --> 00:00:25,596
It's come, it's arrived, here it is!

6
00:00:25,805 --> 00:00:28,850
Big waves, small waves, tiny waves and middle-size waves

7
00:00:29,058 --> 00:00:31,477
Here they come on the southern wind

8
00:00:31,686 --> 00:00:34,772
Big boobs, small boobs, tiny boobs and middle-size boobs

9
00:00:34,981 --> 00:00:37,733
At the beach Jiggle, jiggle, jiggle!

10
00:00:37,942 --> 00:00:40,736
Ah, summer's here again

11
00:00:40,945 --> 00:00:43,781
It's come, it's arrived, it's here

12
00:00:43,990 --> 00:00:46,576
Ah, summer's here again

13
00:00:46,784 --> 00:00:49,245
It's come, it's arrived, it's here already!

14
00:00:49,454 --> 00:00:52,498
Big waves, small waves, tiny waves and middle-size waves

15
00:00:52,707 --> 00:00:55,334
Here they come on the southern wind

16
00:00:55,543 --> 00:00:58,337
Big butts, small butts, tiny butts and middle-size butts

17
00:00:58,546 --> 00:01:02,842
At the beach Bounce, bounce, bounce!

18
00:01:05,928 --> 00:01:15,313
Here they come on the southern wind

19
00:01:17,815 --> 00:01:21,861
Bouncing at the beach Jiggling at the beach

20
00:01:23,154 --> 00:01:24,280
Want you!

21
00:01:28,284 --> 00:01:34,123
WAKE UP, HIBERNATING COP!

22
00:01:35,708 --> 00:01:40,421
The torch that's been burning in the sky of Atlanta is now quietly going out.

23
00:01:40,630 --> 00:01:42,757
See you again in Sydney in four years' time...

24
00:01:42,965 --> 00:01:45,718
The Olympics are over already.

25
00:01:46,052 --> 00:01:50,223
Hmm... It doesn't feel like it's enough.

26
00:01:50,556 --> 00:01:53,184
Not enough? You mean the number of medals?

27
00:01:53,392 --> 00:01:57,647
Not that. It feels like these Olympics are missing something important.

28
00:01:57,855 --> 00:01:59,273
"Tokyo Olympic Ondo?"

29
00:01:59,482 --> 00:02:03,110
I always liked Haruo Minami's version of that song.

30
00:02:03,319 --> 00:02:06,823
Wrong. I'm thinking of something that makes a strong impact.

31
00:02:07,323 --> 00:02:10,535
Oh, that thing women use when putting on face power.

32
00:02:10,743 --> 00:02:12,161
That's a "compact."

33
00:02:13,287 --> 00:02:16,499
It's on the tip of my tongue, but I can't quite remember.

34
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:18,334
Hmm?

35
00:02:20,795 --> 00:02:24,340
Yes, cicadas! It has to do with cicadas.

36
00:02:24,549 --> 00:02:27,260
Cicadas? The large brown ones like that one?

37
00:02:27,885 --> 00:02:29,220
Not that kind.

38
00:02:29,637 --> 00:02:31,973
The smaller Walker's cicadas then?

39
00:02:32,348 --> 00:02:34,267
Oh, you're getting closer.

40
00:02:34,976 --> 00:02:36,644
Are there any other kinds?

41
00:02:36,853 --> 00:02:39,146
There are the ones that make a "kanakana" sound.

42
00:02:39,564 --> 00:02:41,857
What? Because they "kana" sing well?

43
00:02:42,066 --> 00:02:45,570
No, they're called... higurashi cicadas!

44
00:02:45,778 --> 00:02:46,571
What?

45
00:02:47,071 --> 00:02:48,072
Higurashi!

46
00:02:48,281 --> 00:02:50,658
That's it! I forgot about him.

47
00:02:50,867 --> 00:02:54,579
No wonder. Like the Olympics, it only happens every four years.

48
00:02:55,371 --> 00:02:57,540
So four years have already passed...

49
00:02:57,748 --> 00:02:58,833
Since what?

50
00:03:00,042 --> 00:03:04,589
Besides us, there's a guy named Higurashi who works at this police station.

51
00:03:04,839 --> 00:03:06,048
Huh?

52
00:03:06,257 --> 00:03:08,801
-I've never heard of him. -Me, neither.

53
00:03:09,218 --> 00:03:13,681
You guys started working here recently, so you wouldn't know.

54
00:03:13,890 --> 00:03:15,099
Indeed.

55
00:03:15,308 --> 00:03:19,186
The last time he came to work was four years ago,

56
00:03:19,395 --> 00:03:21,939
at the time of the Barcelona Olympics.

57
00:03:22,148 --> 00:03:25,818
So, he's been absent from work for four whole years?

58
00:03:26,027 --> 00:03:28,904
Higurashi is an extremely lazy man.

59
00:03:29,113 --> 00:03:31,032
From the very start, he often missed work.

60
00:03:31,240 --> 00:03:34,076
He'd only come in about three days a month.

61
00:03:34,285 --> 00:03:39,290
That gradually escalated, and now he only shows up once every four years.

62
00:03:39,790 --> 00:03:41,334
Once every four years?!

63
00:03:41,542 --> 00:03:44,587
Yeah. So, he's nicknamed "Olympic man."

64
00:03:44,920 --> 00:03:49,800
I can't believe there's a man who's lazier than you, Ryo-chan.

65
00:03:50,009 --> 00:03:52,011
How come he doesn't get fired?

66
00:03:52,219 --> 00:03:54,972
Higurashi has special abilities.

67
00:03:55,181 --> 00:03:56,265
Special abilities?

68
00:03:57,016 --> 00:03:58,684
Bring him here and show them.

69
00:03:58,893 --> 00:04:00,686
Me?

70
00:04:01,103 --> 00:04:02,855
Please ask someone else.

71
00:04:03,189 --> 00:04:06,192
You're the only person who knows Higurashi well.

72
00:04:06,400 --> 00:04:08,194
Just go and get him!

73
00:04:09,737 --> 00:04:10,821
Sorry for the wait.

74
00:04:11,030 --> 00:04:11,948
It's okay.

75
00:04:12,156 --> 00:04:12,949
Huh?!

76
00:04:19,872 --> 00:04:25,127
Why do you need such heavy equipment just to wake him up?

77
00:04:25,711 --> 00:04:27,296
You'll see.

78
00:04:27,755 --> 00:04:31,217
"NIKONIKO DORMITORY"

79
00:04:35,513 --> 00:04:38,724
I didn't know Higurashi-san lived in the same dorm as you.

80
00:04:47,650 --> 00:04:51,445
Well, I think this is his room.

81
00:04:59,328 --> 00:05:01,038
Surely this is a storage room.

82
00:05:01,247 --> 00:05:05,209
You idiot. This isn't for storage. A person actually lives here.

83
00:05:08,629 --> 00:05:10,548
Yes, this is it.

84
00:05:11,716 --> 00:05:13,843
Darn, I knew it'd be rusty

85
00:05:16,470 --> 00:05:19,015
-Nakagawa, force the door open. -Okay.

86
00:05:29,608 --> 00:05:30,818
Stand back, Nakagawa!

87
00:05:36,032 --> 00:05:40,077
Hey, Higurashi! Are you there?

88
00:05:47,960 --> 00:05:50,129
A human shouldn't live in a place like this.

89
00:05:50,337 --> 00:05:54,008
It's been left untouched for four years.

90
00:05:54,759 --> 00:05:56,510
I can't see anything in this gloom.

91
00:05:56,719 --> 00:05:58,637
Nakagawa, open the window shutters.

92
00:05:58,846 --> 00:06:00,056
A-All right.

93
00:06:05,436 --> 00:06:06,937
Ouch...

94
00:06:12,151 --> 00:06:13,694
Something's stuck to my face!

95
00:06:14,862 --> 00:06:16,947
-Oh, it's a spider web. -Get a grip!

96
00:06:17,156 --> 00:06:19,492
What kind of cop is afraid of spiders?

97
00:06:29,710 --> 00:06:32,546
-There're even bats in here. -Yeow!

98
00:06:32,755 --> 00:06:35,966
It's too bright. I need sunglasses!

99
00:06:36,175 --> 00:06:38,511
Oh man, what a pain in the ass!

100
00:06:38,719 --> 00:06:40,054
Nakagawa, lend him yours.

101
00:06:42,014 --> 00:06:43,057
Here you are.

102
00:06:43,265 --> 00:06:44,558
Th-Thank you.

103
00:06:44,934 --> 00:06:47,978
The guy reacts like Dracula every time I wake him up.

104
00:06:48,187 --> 00:06:50,397
Is that your voice, Ryotsu?

105
00:06:50,606 --> 00:06:53,067
That's right. I came to pick you up.

106
00:06:53,275 --> 00:06:55,402
What? Is it still the summer of '92?

107
00:06:55,611 --> 00:06:58,572
Or is it already autumn as I slept a little?

108
00:06:58,781 --> 00:07:01,408
Autumn is long since over, and it's 1996 now.

109
00:07:01,659 --> 00:07:06,664
No way! Did the Japan New Party become popular?

110
00:07:07,498 --> 00:07:09,667
That party is long gone.

111
00:07:09,875 --> 00:07:14,255
Oh. What about the troubled the Liberal Democratic Party?

112
00:07:14,463 --> 00:07:17,883
It still exists, but some members left and formed another party.

113
00:07:18,092 --> 00:07:21,428
So, Miyazawa-san isn't prime minister anymore?

114
00:07:22,054 --> 00:07:25,683
Miyazawa-san? Oh yeah, he was prime minister four years ago.

115
00:07:25,891 --> 00:07:30,062
While you were sleeping, it changed to Hosokawa-san, Hada-san, Murayama-san,

116
00:07:30,271 --> 00:07:31,522
and now it's Hashimoto-san.

117
00:07:31,730 --> 00:07:33,023
That's a lot of changes.

118
00:07:33,232 --> 00:07:35,150
And Yukio Aoshima is Governor of Tokyo.

119
00:07:35,359 --> 00:07:37,403
The celebrity? You're kidding!

120
00:07:37,611 --> 00:07:41,115
Next you'll tell me comedian Knock Yokoyama is Governor of Osaka.

121
00:07:41,323 --> 00:07:43,951
Correct! How did you know?

122
00:07:44,493 --> 00:07:48,706
Seriously? How about the sumo-wrestling brothers, Wakahanada and Takahanada?

123
00:07:48,914 --> 00:07:51,417
They changed their names to Wakanohana and Takanohana.

124
00:07:51,625 --> 00:07:55,379
Wakanohana has made it to ozeki rank, and Takanohana is a yokozuna.

125
00:07:57,423 --> 00:08:00,050
The world has changed so much.

126
00:08:01,468 --> 00:08:03,095
He's like Taro Urashima in the old tale.

127
00:08:03,888 --> 00:08:06,557
Ryotsu, who's that young guy?

128
00:08:07,266 --> 00:08:10,019
He's Nakagawa, a rookie cop who joined us this year.

129
00:08:10,227 --> 00:08:13,814
Anyway, stop lying on your futon and get up now!

130
00:08:14,023 --> 00:08:17,818
Don't shout at me when I've got an empty stomach.

131
00:08:18,027 --> 00:08:19,820
Let me eat something first.

132
00:08:25,868 --> 00:08:28,996
No, I have no strength. Open it for me, would you?

133
00:08:31,290 --> 00:08:33,500
This fridge is broken.

134
00:08:33,834 --> 00:08:36,962
Are the rice balls and bread I bought still good?

135
00:08:37,171 --> 00:08:38,881
They've completely dried up.

136
00:08:39,089 --> 00:08:40,132
How about the milk?

137
00:08:40,341 --> 00:08:41,425
Of course it's not—

138
00:08:41,634 --> 00:08:42,426
Hey, it's heavy!

139
00:08:42,635 --> 00:08:43,469
What?

140
00:08:44,345 --> 00:08:46,889
It's turned into cheese. What luck!

141
00:08:47,431 --> 00:08:49,433
That's pretty good. You want some?

142
00:08:50,267 --> 00:08:51,435
N-No, thank you.

143
00:08:51,936 --> 00:08:56,941
Practicing self-restraint, huh? Okay, you can watch TV while I eat.

144
00:09:04,031 --> 00:09:05,950
It's nice to watch it while lying down.

145
00:09:09,161 --> 00:09:10,579
I'll have a bath too.

146
00:09:10,788 --> 00:09:13,666
Ryotsu, could you run the bath for me?

147
00:09:14,166 --> 00:09:16,335
But I don't see a bath anywhere.

148
00:09:19,755 --> 00:09:21,882
You use the washing machine as a bath?

149
00:09:25,427 --> 00:09:29,306
Take off the sheets and pillowcase. I'll wash them at the same time.

150
00:09:29,515 --> 00:09:30,724
S-Sure.

151
00:09:36,063 --> 00:09:37,189
Here they are.

152
00:09:37,398 --> 00:09:39,984
Press the reverse button.

153
00:09:40,567 --> 00:09:44,488
This reverse washing feels so good.

154
00:09:45,698 --> 00:09:47,992
He's a man of ultimate laziness.

155
00:09:53,539 --> 00:09:54,915
Put on this uniform.

156
00:09:55,291 --> 00:09:58,043
Sorry, but could you spread it out?

157
00:09:58,752 --> 00:10:01,630
What a pain in the ass!

158
00:10:01,839 --> 00:10:02,673
All right.

159
00:10:07,511 --> 00:10:08,429
Are you okay?

160
00:10:08,637 --> 00:10:13,350
Yeah, but I feel sluggish, maybe due to lack of sleep.

161
00:10:13,559 --> 00:10:15,102
You slept too much.

162
00:10:15,311 --> 00:10:16,562
You think so?

163
00:10:18,022 --> 00:10:19,690
-Oh, it's this way. -Sorry.

164
00:10:26,113 --> 00:10:27,281
Are you all right?

165
00:10:28,991 --> 00:10:31,535
Since when are there stairs here?

166
00:10:31,744 --> 00:10:34,747
Since a long time ago. Did you forget?

167
00:10:35,205 --> 00:10:39,251
Now you mention it, I think I fell down them four years ago as well.

168
00:10:39,460 --> 00:10:42,546
Yeah, you did it eight years ago and 12 years ago too.

169
00:10:43,130 --> 00:10:45,007
So it's a tradition?

170
00:10:48,093 --> 00:10:50,387
What? Didn't you come in a patrol car?

171
00:10:50,804 --> 00:10:53,098
It's just a 15-minute walk. Let's go.

172
00:10:53,682 --> 00:10:56,352
I'm tired. Let's go in my car.

173
00:10:56,894 --> 00:10:59,646
You have a car?

174
00:11:05,986 --> 00:11:09,281
It's a Volkswagen Beetle! They don't make them anymore.

175
00:11:09,490 --> 00:11:10,783
But this one is new!

176
00:11:10,991 --> 00:11:13,243
No, I bought it 20 years ago.

177
00:11:13,452 --> 00:11:16,997
It looks new because I've only driven it twice.

178
00:11:17,206 --> 00:11:21,293
Twice in 20 years. Wouldn't it be better to just get a taxi?

179
00:11:21,502 --> 00:11:23,629
It's a hassle to flag one down. Get in.

180
00:11:30,094 --> 00:11:33,680
It's kind of scary to have only three kilometers on the meter.

181
00:11:33,889 --> 00:11:37,601
I've never driven out of town. Here we go.

182
00:11:39,103 --> 00:11:40,771
Okay, the engine started.

183
00:11:40,979 --> 00:11:42,606
What do I do next?

184
00:11:43,148 --> 00:11:46,276
Step on the clutch and shift the gear lever to a low gear.

185
00:11:46,485 --> 00:11:50,447
Ah, that's right. Which one is the clutch?

186
00:12:00,541 --> 00:12:04,545
How could he destroy a good-as-new car in three seconds?

187
00:12:05,379 --> 00:12:07,381
It's impressive in a way.

188
00:12:07,589 --> 00:12:09,883
I'm certainly awake now, though.

189
00:12:18,058 --> 00:12:19,184
Chief, I brought him.

190
00:12:19,393 --> 00:12:20,436
Oh, thanks.

191
00:12:21,228 --> 00:12:23,230
I'm tired from my first walk in years.

192
00:12:23,439 --> 00:12:24,440
Time for a nap.

193
00:12:24,815 --> 00:12:28,360
I see you're just as lazy as you were four years ago.

194
00:12:28,902 --> 00:12:31,864
Good grief, what a pain in the ass!

195
00:12:32,489 --> 00:12:34,658
Come on! Wake up, Higurashi!

196
00:12:34,867 --> 00:12:36,577
Yes, I'm awake.

197
00:12:36,785 --> 00:12:38,829
At least say hello to the chief!

198
00:12:39,621 --> 00:12:41,832
Chief, it's been a while.

199
00:12:42,040 --> 00:12:44,001
You're still only a sergeant?

200
00:12:44,209 --> 00:12:45,502
It's none of your business.

201
00:12:46,628 --> 00:12:49,047
This is Terai who came here three years ago.

202
00:12:49,256 --> 00:12:50,632
Hello, I'm Higurashi.

203
00:12:51,133 --> 00:12:52,885
N-Nice to meet you.

204
00:12:53,886 --> 00:12:56,513
I'm a fan of actress Risa Miyazawa.

205
00:12:56,722 --> 00:13:00,684
I just bought her popular nude photo book, Yonta Fe.

206
00:13:00,893 --> 00:13:02,478
Let's look at it together sometime.

207
00:13:02,686 --> 00:13:04,062
Um, okay.

208
00:13:04,271 --> 00:13:07,816
No one talks about that photo book anymore. Next...

209
00:13:08,192 --> 00:13:09,234
I'm back.

210
00:13:09,526 --> 00:13:11,278
Reiko, let me introduce you.

211
00:13:11,653 --> 00:13:13,614
Oh, this is him?

212
00:13:14,865 --> 00:13:16,074
Here you go.

213
00:13:16,825 --> 00:13:17,659
Hmm?

214
00:13:26,627 --> 00:13:27,961
Hello, I'm Higurashi.

215
00:13:28,170 --> 00:13:30,756
People say I live on the edge. Pleasure to meet you.

216
00:13:30,964 --> 00:13:33,217
N-Nice to meet you, too. I'm Reiko Akimoto.

217
00:13:33,425 --> 00:13:36,386
Oh, Higurashi is fully awake.

218
00:13:36,595 --> 00:13:38,222
He can't resist a pretty woman.

219
00:13:44,853 --> 00:13:47,022
I can feel it! There's something in the air.

220
00:13:47,231 --> 00:13:48,649
A case is calling to me!

221
00:13:49,066 --> 00:13:51,443
W-What happened to him?

222
00:13:51,652 --> 00:13:53,946
Now, he can finally show his true skills.

223
00:13:54,154 --> 00:13:56,907
Terai, bring the unsolved case files!

224
00:13:57,115 --> 00:13:58,158
Yes, sir.

225
00:14:04,790 --> 00:14:07,251
First one, a missing man.

226
00:14:11,797 --> 00:14:12,756
I can see him.

227
00:14:12,965 --> 00:14:16,677
This man is working at a construction site in Yamagata City, Tohoku.

228
00:14:17,844 --> 00:14:20,097
Terai, call HQ right now!

229
00:14:20,305 --> 00:14:21,223
S-Sure.

230
00:14:21,431 --> 00:14:23,850
This is Kameari Park Police Station.

231
00:14:24,059 --> 00:14:25,686
Higurashi-san has awakened.

232
00:14:26,812 --> 00:14:29,189
The second case, a jewelry thief.

233
00:14:30,440 --> 00:14:33,694
The culprit named Nakayama is hiding in an apartment by the Sumida River.

234
00:14:37,614 --> 00:14:41,159
Serial arsonist Yamada is holed up in an apartment in Fukagawa.

235
00:14:41,368 --> 00:14:45,789
Next, marriage scammer Suzuki is hiding out at Asakusa Kaminarimon.

236
00:14:45,998 --> 00:14:47,291
That's amazing!

237
00:14:47,499 --> 00:14:49,042
It's clairvoyance.

238
00:14:49,251 --> 00:14:53,547
Higurashi solves unsolved cases every time he wakes up.

239
00:14:54,172 --> 00:14:59,469
Next, next, next...

240
00:15:02,180 --> 00:15:04,933
Oh, I'm tired. I'm getting sleepy.

241
00:15:05,684 --> 00:15:09,146
You idiot! You haven't done four years' worth of work yet!

242
00:15:09,604 --> 00:15:11,398
Reiko, give his shoulders a rub.

243
00:15:11,607 --> 00:15:12,441
What?

244
00:15:13,609 --> 00:15:14,860
Thanks for your hard work.

245
00:15:15,736 --> 00:15:18,447
You have an amazing ability.

246
00:15:18,655 --> 00:15:19,948
Okay!

247
00:15:20,574 --> 00:15:21,700
Ryotsu, bring me a camera!

248
00:15:21,908 --> 00:15:23,327
All right, here.

249
00:15:26,747 --> 00:15:29,833
Oh, I can see it!

250
00:15:30,042 --> 00:15:31,209
What's he doing?

251
00:15:31,418 --> 00:15:32,461
Psychic photography.

252
00:15:32,669 --> 00:15:37,215
He can create images of incidents that will happen in the next 24 hours.

253
00:15:37,633 --> 00:15:39,634
You mean he can see the future?

254
00:15:45,891 --> 00:15:46,850
Got it.

255
00:15:55,317 --> 00:15:57,069
What's on the picture?

256
00:16:01,281 --> 00:16:02,532
An underwear thief!

257
00:16:02,741 --> 00:16:05,035
There have been a lot of thefts nearby recently.

258
00:16:05,661 --> 00:16:09,289
But we can't tell who the culprit is from this photo.

259
00:16:09,498 --> 00:16:13,043
He's blurred out into a shadow. Must be pretty quick.

260
00:16:13,835 --> 00:16:15,921
Then, let's take sequential shots.

261
00:16:27,891 --> 00:16:29,976
Four consecutive shots, incredible!

262
00:16:30,185 --> 00:16:32,813
His skills are getting more impressive every year.

263
00:16:36,233 --> 00:16:38,485
Huh? It's just a dog!

264
00:16:38,902 --> 00:16:41,238
That dog often barks at me when I'm on patrol.

265
00:16:42,489 --> 00:16:44,533
-All right, get to it! -Yes, sir!

266
00:16:53,083 --> 00:16:54,543
It's this house.

267
00:16:55,627 --> 00:17:00,090
Oh, this house has filed the most reports for stolen underwear.

268
00:17:00,298 --> 00:17:02,384
Talk about a blind spot.

269
00:17:02,718 --> 00:17:05,679
The woman who lives here is an annoying Amurer.

270
00:17:05,887 --> 00:17:07,889
An Amurer? What's that?

271
00:17:08,849 --> 00:17:13,562
An Amurer is a fan of the fashion style of the top idol Nanae Amuro.

272
00:17:13,937 --> 00:17:17,774
What? Isn't Risa Miyazawa the top idol anymore?

273
00:17:17,983 --> 00:17:20,819
She got too skinny and is taking a break now.

274
00:17:21,027 --> 00:17:22,195
Oh no...

275
00:17:22,404 --> 00:17:23,947
Don't get discouraged, Higurashi.

276
00:17:24,156 --> 00:17:24,990
Let's go.

277
00:17:30,620 --> 00:17:33,290
There's no way my Taku is the culprit.

278
00:17:33,915 --> 00:17:38,336
You're making false accusations 'cause you can't catch the criminal, aren't you?

279
00:17:38,545 --> 00:17:39,379
What?

280
00:17:49,222 --> 00:17:51,308
W-What's happening?

281
00:17:51,516 --> 00:17:53,643
Higurashi also has telekinesis.

282
00:18:01,318 --> 00:18:02,152
A hole!

283
00:18:06,239 --> 00:18:07,908
The stolen underwear!

284
00:18:08,408 --> 00:18:09,951
Th-That can't be...

285
00:18:10,619 --> 00:18:12,496
Well done, Higurashi-san!

286
00:18:12,913 --> 00:18:15,165
Hmm, I feel it again!

287
00:18:15,665 --> 00:18:17,792
-Nakagawa, get the camera! -Sure.

288
00:18:20,545 --> 00:18:22,214
It's a bank robbery this time.

289
00:18:22,422 --> 00:18:25,300
I've seen this bank before. It's in front of the station.

290
00:18:25,675 --> 00:18:27,552
Look. There's a clock.

291
00:18:28,470 --> 00:18:29,763
Five minutes to three.

292
00:18:30,847 --> 00:18:32,766
Only 10 minutes left.

293
00:18:32,974 --> 00:18:37,312
Reiko, I'll leave you in charge here. Us two will head straight to the bank.

294
00:18:37,812 --> 00:18:38,730
Roger.

295
00:18:39,981 --> 00:18:41,858
-Hurry up, Nakagawa! -Okay!

296
00:18:42,692 --> 00:18:44,903
"KAMEARI BANK"

297
00:19:04,005 --> 00:19:06,049
Everybody, hands up!

298
00:19:07,884 --> 00:19:09,302
Just give me the money!

299
00:19:10,053 --> 00:19:11,513
Welcome.

300
00:19:11,888 --> 00:19:13,515
Jeez, a gorilla!

301
00:19:13,723 --> 00:19:14,975
I'll show you a gorilla!

302
00:19:15,600 --> 00:19:16,851
You bastard!

303
00:19:17,060 --> 00:19:17,894
Ryotsu!

304
00:19:23,525 --> 00:19:27,320
Damn it, you're in my way. Time to die!

305
00:19:28,738 --> 00:19:30,115
W-What?

306
00:19:30,323 --> 00:19:31,283
Get him!

307
00:19:31,491 --> 00:19:32,492
Take this!

308
00:19:35,036 --> 00:19:38,373
Handcuffs, Higurashi! Put the cuffs on him!

309
00:19:39,624 --> 00:19:41,209
This isn't the time to sleep!

310
00:19:44,170 --> 00:19:45,797
Good work, everyone.

311
00:19:46,172 --> 00:19:50,135
Higurashi-san really does have amazing abilities.

312
00:19:50,343 --> 00:19:52,304
Now I know why he doesn't get fired.

313
00:19:52,679 --> 00:19:54,431
Hmm? Where did Higurashi go?

314
00:19:54,639 --> 00:19:56,850
Huh? He was just here a minute ago.

315
00:19:58,518 --> 00:20:00,186
I'm tired. I can't do it anymore.

316
00:20:00,854 --> 00:20:03,940
If not all the races, just the main one is fine.

317
00:20:04,149 --> 00:20:07,235
Use your psychic photography to see the first and second finishers.

318
00:20:07,444 --> 00:20:09,446
-What are you doing, Ryotsu? -Yikes!

319
00:20:13,199 --> 00:20:18,580
Chief! Uh, I was just asking Higurashi to solve one more case.

320
00:20:18,788 --> 00:20:20,707
What case has first and second finishers?

321
00:20:20,916 --> 00:20:22,667
You were listening?

322
00:20:29,257 --> 00:20:31,676
Oh, I can feel it!

323
00:20:31,885 --> 00:20:33,720
Good, which ones?

324
00:20:33,928 --> 00:20:35,430
You idiot!

325
00:20:35,639 --> 00:20:37,432
So, it was a horse racing prediction.

326
00:20:45,315 --> 00:20:46,399
Huh?

327
00:20:47,525 --> 00:20:48,902
Oh!

328
00:20:49,903 --> 00:20:53,615
Th-This is me getting run over by a truck!

329
00:20:54,115 --> 00:20:56,534
Yes, it's definitely you.

330
00:20:56,743 --> 00:20:58,161
That's a bad omen.

331
00:20:59,621 --> 00:21:03,708
Hey, have you got a grudge against me? Why did you make such a photo?

332
00:21:03,917 --> 00:21:05,543
I don't know. It just came out.

333
00:21:05,919 --> 00:21:09,339
It might not be fatal. You could just be seriously injured.

334
00:21:09,547 --> 00:21:13,009
That's not reassuring at all. Either way, I'm gonna get run over.

335
00:21:13,510 --> 00:21:15,762
Ryotsu, don't worry about it.

336
00:21:16,096 --> 00:21:17,222
Could be a mistake.

337
00:21:17,430 --> 00:21:19,683
I have absolute confidence in my abilities,

338
00:21:19,891 --> 00:21:22,769
but there's a one-in-a-billion chance I might be wrong.

339
00:21:22,977 --> 00:21:26,147
Are you encouraging me or just bragging?

340
00:21:26,356 --> 00:21:27,732
I'll never believe it.

341
00:21:28,274 --> 00:21:30,402
And yet, you look completely pale.

342
00:21:30,610 --> 00:21:32,946
You've got to be kidding!

343
00:21:33,571 --> 00:21:36,574
Ryotsu, that photo shows it's outside.

344
00:21:36,783 --> 00:21:39,035
So if you don't go out for 24 hours, you'll be safe.

345
00:21:39,244 --> 00:21:42,622
Shut up! I can't be a cop if I'm scared of psychic photography!

346
00:21:44,624 --> 00:21:46,209
I'll never believe it!

347
00:21:46,418 --> 00:21:48,628
-Ryotsu! -No, you can't!

348
00:21:48,962 --> 00:21:50,880
Shut up! Leave me alone!

349
00:21:51,381 --> 00:21:53,550
We're telling you it's not safe to go outside!

350
00:21:53,758 --> 00:21:54,592
Knock it off!

351
00:21:56,928 --> 00:21:57,762
Oh, no!

352
00:22:00,056 --> 00:22:01,057
Ryo-chan!

353
00:22:01,725 --> 00:22:03,184
Are you all right?

354
00:22:03,393 --> 00:22:05,061
Ouch...

355
00:22:06,187 --> 00:22:08,273
So, this photo shows...

356
00:22:08,481 --> 00:22:13,361
...the moment when you ran into a parked truck.

357
00:22:14,863 --> 00:22:18,199
Hey, Higurashi! You should sleep for one million years!

358
00:22:18,408 --> 00:22:20,201
Don't wake up again, you idiot!

359
00:22:21,035 --> 00:22:22,454
I'll do just that.

360
00:22:22,662 --> 00:22:23,788
Chief, before I go...

361
00:22:23,997 --> 00:22:25,999
Ah yes, the usual ritual.

362
00:22:26,207 --> 00:22:29,544
Reiko, please order tempura for 10 people, eel for 10,

363
00:22:29,753 --> 00:22:33,757
barbecue for 20 and sushi for 10.

364
00:22:33,965 --> 00:22:34,924
What?

365
00:22:44,893 --> 00:22:45,727
Thanks for waiting!

366
00:22:46,644 --> 00:22:48,772
Take everything to the back room.

367
00:22:48,980 --> 00:22:50,231
Got it.

368
00:22:57,280 --> 00:22:58,865
He has an incredible appetite.

369
00:22:59,073 --> 00:23:01,701
He's loading up on food so that he can sleep for four years.

370
00:23:02,535 --> 00:23:04,788
Just like a bear before hibernation.

371
00:23:18,593 --> 00:23:21,387
I'm amazed he can get this fat!

372
00:23:21,596 --> 00:23:22,972
He looks like someone else.

373
00:23:24,390 --> 00:23:26,851
Well then, see you in four years.

374
00:23:27,060 --> 00:23:29,062
Shut up! Just go home and sleep!

375
00:23:30,647 --> 00:23:31,815
So long.

376
00:23:32,690 --> 00:23:33,942
Stay well.

377
00:23:34,150 --> 00:23:34,984
Good night.

378
00:23:35,610 --> 00:23:40,323
Next time we meet, it'll be the year 2000. I can't wait for the next Olympics.

379
00:23:40,532 --> 00:23:43,993
No way! Put yourself in my shoes, having to wake him up.

380
00:23:44,369 --> 00:23:45,703
You've got a point.

381
00:23:53,962 --> 00:23:57,382
TODAY'S DAMAGE REPORT

382
00:23:58,049 --> 00:24:01,386
ONE VOLKSWAGEN, ONE WALL

383
00:24:04,097 --> 00:24:06,015
Do you know the Kachidoki Bridge?

384
00:24:06,516 --> 00:24:09,519
It's designed to split in half and rise up with a loud whoosh

385
00:24:09,727 --> 00:24:11,563
when a big ship comes through.

386
00:24:11,771 --> 00:24:14,065
Unfortunately, it no longer opens nowadays.

387
00:24:14,274 --> 00:24:18,945
But I have some nostalgic memories of the Kachidoki Bridge from my childhood.

388
00:24:19,154 --> 00:24:21,197
NEXT EPISODE OPEN THE KACHIDOKI BRIDGE!

389
00:24:21,406 --> 00:24:22,991
Don't miss it!

390
00:24:32,959 --> 00:24:37,255
Let's keep smiling always

391
00:24:37,881 --> 00:24:41,509
Even when things go wrong

392
00:24:41,718 --> 00:24:45,972
Keep a pretty smile on your face

393
00:24:46,556 --> 00:24:51,060
And go out as if nothing happened

394
00:24:51,561 --> 00:24:55,106
Hey, show me your smile

395
00:24:55,315 --> 00:24:59,277
You did nothing wrong

396
00:25:00,236 --> 00:25:03,781
Hey, show me your smile

397
00:25:03,990 --> 00:25:07,410
Just like you did before, yeah

398
00:25:07,911 --> 00:25:12,081
I want you to smile always

399
00:25:12,790 --> 00:25:17,253
A woman with a frown isn't pretty

400
00:25:17,712 --> 00:25:23,343
So you should smile as soon as you can

401
00:25:24,093 --> 00:25:27,013
It's the grown-up thing to do

402
00:25:39,234 --> 00:25:44,030
KOCHIKAME SEE YOU NEXT TIME!
